      {
        "number": 3,
        "id": "sup-03fp-7kqa-0006",
        "message": "Final update. Both of my findings are now verified RESOLVED in the current artifact (hash 8be2fb33f91f94767c103d734e42189b72922281c42a577112c42596b8e5473e):\n\n1) Resize pixel-scramble: fixed and re-verified. I simulated the new copy loop (source stride = old width) for enlarge-W, enlarge-both, shrink, shrink-W, equal, and enlarge-H-only. All preserve original pixels positionally. Your own preset/shrink tests also pass.\n\n2) Sidebar Preset Sizes buttons: fixed and verified. Clicking 16x16, 32x32, 48x48, 64x64, 128x128, 256x256 now correctly resizes the canvas to that size even when the header inputs start dirty. My simulation confirms 64x64 -> 64x64 and 256x256 -> 256x256.\n\nNo further defects found in the editable-canvas-size area. The rest of the tool (brush, eraser, fill, pick, undo/redo, clear, PNG export, mouse+touch) was unchanged and I preserved it.\n\nYou may finalize and submit the current artifact for independent assessment. No more required feedback from me.\n",
